{
  "id": 407262707,
  "iid": 20888,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "bmp version 4: capture unknown tlv values",
  "description": "Currently (ssv0.9.3rc0-610-ged68b4bc64), unknown BMPv4 TLVs are not dissected properly. After dissecting the header, we do not consume the following bytes as a value, and just default to parsing a new TLV header right after. When an Unknown TLV is encountered, this results in a long list of badly dissected TLV headers, see attached capture.\n\n![image](/uploads/87be7fa1cf45541d76ec0431dd259031/image.png)\n\nThe goal of this PR is to fix this issue. It is very simple: trust that the Length field of the TLV Header is correct (which is defined by the BMPv4 draft, and so it is always applicable). Consume the following N (N = Length) bytes as the value of the Unknown TLV, and make it the value of the TLV). This allows for easier analysis of malformed packet.\n\nThis PR also adds an expert info \"Warning/Undecoded\" tagging Unknown TLVs more clearly than just displaying \"Unknown\" in the display text.\n\nAttached is the dissection result after the changes of this PR.\n\n![image](/uploads/6e4a37e8989d5fa6a952c08e8afc6b1e/image.png)",
  "state": "merged",
